# What never gets uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Important: when this file exists Vercel uses it *instead of* .gitignore, not
# in addition to it. Everything that must stay out has to be listed here, which
# is why the dependency and build entries are repeated below rather than left
# to .gitignore.
#
# The entry that matters most is .env: a CLI deploy uploads the working
# directory, so without this line a local .env.local with production secrets
# would travel to the build. Environment variables belong in the Vercel
# project settings, never in the upload.

# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# dependencies and build output (Vercel installs and builds on its side)
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
/src/generated/prisma

# local tooling
.git
.vercel
.vscode
.cursor
*.tsbuildinfo
*.pem
.DS_Store

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
